      "content": "I'll read the original test and the CUT source to understand the code before improving it.Now I understand the original test. Let me write a cleaner, more understandable version that:\n1. Removes the large amount of irrelevant boilerplate (unused methods/fields from parent classes)\n2. Extracts the repeated serialize/deserialize logic into a helper method\n3. Adds clear documentation explaining what is and isn't being tested\n4. Uses try-with-resources for cleaner resource management\n5. Fixes compile issues (undefined `E` type, undefined `isTestSerialization()`, invalid abstract stubs)The `Transformer` interface requires a `transform(String)` method, not `apply()`. I'll fix the method name in `IntegerTransformer`.The test compiles successfully. The fix was changing `apply()` to `transform()` to match the `Transformer` interface's abstract method signature."
